    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Question\n\nHi echasnovski! Is it possible to provide support for `git add -p` in mini.git explictly so that I can interactively stage hunks using `:Git add -p`. I think this would be a great addon since it does not depend on anything other than the installed git. You can also redirect users to use this functionality for staging going forward. Currently when I try `:Git add -p` it prints the output using vim.notify notifications providing no way to interact with it.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.git</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi echasnovski! Is it possible to provide support for <code class=\"notranslate\">git add -p</code> in mini.git explictly so that I can interactively stage hunks using <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git add -p</code>. I think this would be a great addon since it does not depend on anything other than the installed git. You can also redirect users to use this functionality for staging going forward. Currently when I try <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git add -p</code> it prints the output using vim.notify notifications providing no way to interact with it.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.git\nQuestion\nHi echasnovski! Is it possible to provide support for git add -p in mini.git explictly so that I can interactively stage hunks using :Git add -p. I think this would be a great addon since it does not depend on anything other than the installed git. You can also redirect users to use this functionality for staging going forward. Currently when I try :Git add -p it prints the output using vim.notify notifications providing no way to interact with it.",
