            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "In theory it should be possible, of course, but this type of interactive subcommands is [out of scope for 'mini.git'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d90adc96b68b310cf17d8ebcc8e2e4626c6bb8cc/doc/mini-git.txt#L25-L27). The main reason is that I don't see a robust and *concise* programmatic way to detect this type of command and interact with it.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">In theory it should be possible, of course, but this type of interactive subcommands is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d90adc96b68b310cf17d8ebcc8e2e4626c6bb8cc/doc/mini-git.txt#L25-L27\">out of scope for 'mini.git'</a>. The main reason is that I don't see a robust and <em>concise</em> programmatic way to detect this type of command and interact with it.</p>",
            "bodyText": "In theory it should be possible, of course, but this type of interactive subcommands is out of scope for 'mini.git'. The main reason is that I don't see a robust and concise programmatic way to detect this type of command and interact with it.",
