                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "This might work, but I don't think detecting \"these kind of interactive things\" is possible without hardcoding specific command-argument combinations. And even in that case detecting them will not be straightforward, as target arguments can appear in *almost* any place (after `Git` but before `--`).\r\n\r\nSo at the moment I don't think it is worth added complexity.\r\n\r\n",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This might work, but I don't think detecting \"these kind of interactive things\" is possible without hardcoding specific command-argument combinations. And even in that case detecting them will not be straightforward, as target arguments can appear in <em>almost</em> any place (after <code class=\"notranslate\">Git</code> but before <code class=\"notranslate\">--</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So at the moment I don't think it is worth added complexity.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "This might work, but I don't think detecting \"these kind of interactive things\" is possible without hardcoding specific command-argument combinations. And even in that case detecting them will not be straightforward, as target arguments can appear in almost any place (after Git but before --).\nSo at the moment I don't think it is worth added complexity.",
